          "type": "concept",
          "title": "3. Indicators",
          "text": "Indicators are substances whose colour changes in acidic or basic media. Litmus is red in acid and blue in base. Methyl orange is red in acidic solution and yellow in basic solution. Phenolphthalein is colourless in acidic solution and pink in basic solution. Universal indicator gives a broader colour scale associated with pH and is useful when an approximate pH is required."
