          "title": "Test for hydrogen gas",
          "question": "A gas is produced when zinc reacts with dilute hydrochloric acid. How can the gas be identified?",
          "answer": "Collect the gas safely and bring a burning splint near it under controlled laboratory conditions. Hydrogen burns with a characteristic pop sound. The reaction is Zn + 2HCl → ZnCl₂ + H₂."
